-- coa22-part32.l4: Part 32 (Company investigations: amendments) of the Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), ss 1035 to
-- 1039 (lines 14531-14621 of ukpga-2006-46.txt). LAYER 1: the law, objectively.
--
-- WHAT IS ENCODED. Part 32 amends Part 14 of the Companies Act 1985. The instructions that amend ("insert",
-- "substitute", "omit", "cease to have effect") are INERT, reason 2 (amendments of other Acts), and are quoted below
-- without a rule. The text those instructions insert or substitute states rules about inspectors appointed to
-- investigate a company and about the Secretary of State's directions to them, and that text is ENCODED: sections 446A
-- to 446E of the 1985 Act (inserted by ss 1035 to 1037) and subsections (6) to (8) of its section 434 and (9) of its
-- section 447 (substituted by s 1038). Each function is named for the section of THIS Act that inserts the text, then
-- the 1985 section: `s 1035 s 446A(1) ...`. These provisions address the Secretary of State, inspectors and former
-- inspectors, not a company's directors or members: there is no seat for an official (NOTES.md says so).
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; it is not the
-- official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text". Quote lines are copied from it by a
-- script and checked by srcrefs.py.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer; see NOTES.md).
--   JUST TRUE   the text says the case is within the rule.
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words ("only", "unless", "where", "means", a flat negative).
--   NOTHING     the text does not decide (silent, list not closed, includes, undefined term, points outside the
--               text, limited by its own wording).
--   Each such branch carries  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<words>"  or  -- NOTHING-kind (<why>).
-- Facts a witness can state, and judgments the text hands to the Secretary of State ("it appears to him"), are BOOLEAN
-- inputs. Sections 431, 432, 433, 437 and 442 of the 1985 Act, and section 446A(3), are cited, not encoded here.

§ `Part 32 -- Company investigations: amendments`

-- ---- s 1035: Powers of Secretary of State to give directions to inspectors ------------------------------------------

-- (1) In Part 14 of the Companies Act 1985, after section 446 insert the new sections 446A and 446B (their text is
-- below). The instruction is inert, reason 2.
-- src:14533 | (1) In Part 14 of the Companies Act 1985 (c. 6) (investigation of companies and their affairs), after section 446 insert—
-- src:14534 | Powers of Secretary of State to give directions to inspectors
§§ `s 1035(1) the instruction to insert sections 446A and 446B (inert: amendment of another Act)`

-- 446A(1) In exercising his functions an inspector shall comply with any direction given to him by the Secretary of
-- State under this section.
-- src:14536 | (1) In exercising his functions an inspector shall comply with any direction given to him by the Secretary of State under this section.
@ref s 1035 s 446A(1) General powers to give directions (src:14536)
GIVEN `the direction is given to the inspector by the Secretary of State under section 446A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1035 s 446A(1) the inspector must comply with the direction` MEANS
    IF `the direction is given to the inspector by the Secretary of State under section 446A`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an inspector shall comply with any direction given to him by the Secretary of State under this section"; the case is not mentioned


-- 446A(2) The Secretary of State may give an inspector appointed under section 431, 432(2) or 442(1) a direction (a) as
-- to the subject matter of his investigation, or (b) which requires the inspector to take or not to take a specified
-- step in his investigation.
-- src:14537 | (2) The Secretary of State may give an inspector appointed under section 431, 432(2) or 442(1) a direction—
-- src:14538 | (a) as to the subject matter of his investigation (whether by reference to a specified area of a company's operation, a specified transaction, a period of time or otherwise), or
-- src:14539 | (b) which requires the inspector to take or not to take a specified step in his investigation.
@ref s 1035 s 446A(2) General powers to give directions (src:14537-14539)
GIVEN `the inspector was appointed under section 431, 432(2) or 442(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the direction is as to the subject matter of his investigation (whether by reference to a specified area of a company's operation, a specified transaction, a period of time or otherwise)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the direction requires the inspector to take or not to take a specified step in his investigation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1035 s 446A(2) the Secretary of State may give the inspector the direction` MEANS
    IF     `the inspector was appointed under section 431, 432(2) or 442(1)`
       AND (   `the direction is as to the subject matter of his investigation (whether by reference to a specified area of a company's operation, a specified transaction, a period of time or otherwise)`
            OR `the direction requires the inspector to take or not to take a specified step in his investigation`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Secretary of State may give an inspector appointed under section 431, 432(2) or 442(1) a direction— (a) as to the subject matter of his investigation ... or (b) which requires the inspector to take or not to take a specified step"; another inspector or another direction is not mentioned

-- 446A(3) The Secretary of State may give an inspector appointed under any provision of this Part a direction requiring
-- him to secure that a specified report under section 437 (a) includes the inspector's views on a specified matter,
-- (b) does not include any reference to a specified matter, (c) is made in a specified form or manner, or (d) is made
-- by a specified date.
