§§ `s 1037(1) the instruction to insert section 446E (inert: amendment of another Act)`

-- 446E(1) The section applies to a person who was appointed as an inspector under Part 14 and who (a) has resigned, or
-- (b) whose appointment has been revoked. (2) It also applies to an inspector to whom the Secretary of State has given
-- a direction under section 446B.
-- src:14591 | (1) This section applies to a person who was appointed as an inspector under this Part—
-- src:14592 | (a) who has resigned, or
-- src:14593 | (b) whose appointment has been revoked.
-- src:14594 | (2) This section also applies to an inspector to whom the Secretary of State has given a direction under section 446B (termination of investigation).
@ref s 1037 s 446E(1) Obtaining information from former inspectors etc (src:14591-14594)
GIVEN `the person was appointed as an inspector and has resigned` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was appointed as an inspector and the appointment has been revoked` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an inspector to whom the Secretary of State has given a direction under section 446B (termination of investigation)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1037 s 446E(1) section 446E applies to the person` MEANS
    IF `the person was appointed as an inspector and has resigned` OR `the person was appointed as an inspector and the appointment has been revoked` OR `the person is an inspector to whom the Secretary of State has given a direction under section 446B (termination of investigation)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies to a person who was appointed as an inspector under this Part— (a) who has resigned, or (b) whose appointment has been revoked" and "This section also applies to an inspector to whom the Secretary of State has given a direction under section 446B"; no "only" closes the scope

-- 446E(3) The Secretary of State may direct a person to whom the section applies to produce documents obtained or
-- generated by that person during the course of his investigation to (a) the Secretary of State, or (b) an inspector
-- appointed under Part 14.
-- src:14595 | (3) The Secretary of State may direct a person to whom this section applies to produce documents obtained or generated by that person during the course of his investigation to—
-- src:14596 | (a) the Secretary of State, or
-- src:14597 | (b) an inspector appointed under this Part.
