      `the documents were obtained or generated by that person during the course of his investigation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the documents are to be produced to the Secretary of State or to an inspector appointed under Part 14 of the Companies Act 1985` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1037 s 446E(3) the Secretary of State may direct the person to produce the documents` MEANS
    IF     `s 1037 s 446E(1) section 446E applies to the person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND `the documents were obtained or generated by that person during the course of his investigation`
       AND `the documents are to be produced to the Secretary of State or to an inspector appointed under Part 14 of the Companies Act 1985`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Secretary of State may direct a person to whom this section applies to produce documents obtained or generated by that person during the course of his investigation to— (a) the Secretary of State, or (b) an inspector appointed under this Part"; another direction is not mentioned

